## root
Usage: leaf [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Build and run interactive pages a session shares with its user.

Options:
  --version  Print this running Leaf payload's source version.
  --root     Print the payload directory this leaf runs from.
  --help     Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  codex     Launch Codex and connect Leaf pages to its tasks.
  data      Set or clear page-bound external data.
  delivery  Read input delivered by any Leaf harness.
  package   Create, check, install, and run packages.
  page      Create, check, stamp, and read pages.
  server    Start, run, or stop the local server.
  status    Say the page waits on its user, or is done.
  task      Open, start, or end tasks on the page, yours or the user's.
  thread    Open, answer, edit, summarize, or resolve a thread.
  wait      Confirm a delivery, if given, then wait for the next batch.

## codex
Usage: leaf codex [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Launch Codex or run Leaf's detached delivery carrier.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  launch  Launch an experimental streaming Codex terminal.
  start   Keep PAGE connected after this turn ends.

## data
Usage: leaf data [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Manage each bound source's current value, one JSON file per source.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  clear  Remove one source's current value.
  set    Replace one bound source value.

## package
Usage: leaf package [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Create, check, install, and run packages.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  check    Check a package as one unit.
  init     Create a package directory.
  install  Install a package for selection by name.
  run      Run one of a package's scripts.

## package-init
Usage: leaf package init [OPTIONS] PACKAGE

  Create the package layout without replacing existing files.

  With --widget, add one checked upgraded content widget starter.

Options:
  --widget TAG  add one upgraded content widget starter
  --help        Show this message and exit.

## page
Usage: leaf page [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Create, check, stamp, and read pages.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  check         Check the mutable page source.
  claim         Take a page this session did not serve.
  events        Print the event log as JSON lines.
  export        Export a stamped version to one HTML file.
  init          Create or re-vendor a page directory.
  instructions  Read instructions for selected components and audience.
  media         Add images, video, or audio and print their page paths.
  picture       Picture a drawing comment as the user saw it.
  report        Report a state change onto a page widget, as a worker.
  stamp         Stamp the current source as the next version.
  state         Print where the page, a thread, or a widget stands.
  transcript    Print the page's exchange as Markdown.

## server
Usage: leaf server [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Start, run, or stop the local server.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  run    Serve a page in the foreground until stopped.
  start  Start a page's server and print its URL.
  stop   Stop a page's server.

## thread
Usage: leaf thread [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Open and answer threads as the agent, and maintain them.

  Every write prints the records it appended, one JSON line each, as `page
  events` prints them. `page state PAGE ID` reads one thread.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  edit       Edit a message's text, or its thread's title.
  open       Open an agent thread \u2014 on a passage, or on the page whole.
  reply      Reply to a thread as the agent.
  resolve    Close a thread as the agent.
  summarize  Summarize a contiguous message range.
